    "breakout": "Played Texas honky-tonks for a decade with his Ace in the Hole Band; signed to MCA Records; released 'Unwound' (1981); single-handedly reversed the pop-crossover 'Urban Cowboy' era, restoring traditional fiddle and steel guitar to country music; holds the all-time world record with 60 #1 singles.",
    "avatar_icon": "👑",
    "bio": "The King of Country Music. Respected for pure traditionalism, George Strait never chased pop trends, wearing a crisp cowboy hat and starched Wranglers while delivering timeless Western swing, fiddle-driven shuffles, and heart-aching ballads.",
