    "family": "Grew up in extreme poverty in 'The Battlefield' district of New Orleans; taken in by the Jewish Karnofsky family who bought him his first cornet.",
    "education": "Learned cornet at the Colored Waif's Home for Boys under Peter Davis; mentored by King Oliver in New Orleans brass bands.",
    "breakout": "Joined King Oliver's Creole Jazz Band in Chicago in 1922; recorded the historic Hot Five and Hot Seven sessions (1925–1928) that established the soloist in jazz.",
    "avatar_icon": "🎺",
    "bio": "Affectionately known as 'Satchmo' and 'Pops', Armstrong was the single founding genius of American jazz trumpet and gravel-voiced vocal swing, making scat singing a worldwide art form.",
