    "bio": "With over 220 million records sold and nine #1 hits on Billboard, the Bee Gees became the sonic architects of the disco era with 'Saturday Night Fever', while writing and producing massive hits for Barbra Streisand, Dionne Warwick, and Kenny Rogers.",
